"717",""
"718",""
"719",""
"720",""
"721",""
"722",""
"723","On the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, he said: I have not seen a people better than the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). They did not ask him except about thirteen questions until he passed away, all of which are in the Qurʾān: {They ask you about the sacred month} [Al-Baqarah: 217]. And {They ask you about wine and gambling} [Al-Baqarah: 219]. And {They ask you about orphans} [Al-Baqarah: 220]. And {They ask you about menstruation} [Al-Baqarah: 222]. And {They ask you about the spoils of war} [Al-Anfāl: 1]. And {They ask you what they should spend} [Al-Baqarah: 215]. They did not ask except about what benefits them. He said: And the first to circumambulate the House were the angels. And indeed, what is between the Stone and the Yemeni Corner are graves from the graves of the prophets. A prophet, when his people harmed him, would go out from among them to worship Allah therein until he died.Narrated by Al-Ṭabarānī in Al-Muʿjam Al-Kabīr. In its chain is ʿAṭāʾ ibn Al-Sāʾib, and he is trustworthy but he became confused (in his later years), and the rest of its narrators are trustworthy."
"724",""
"725","On the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) was sitting in the mosque, and they thought that revelation would descend upon him, so they kept away from him, until Abu Dharr came and rushed in and sat with him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) turned to him and said: ""O Abu Dharr, have you prayed today?"" He said: No. He said: ""Stand and pray."" So when he prayed the four rak'ahs of Duha, he turned to him and said: ""O Abu Dharr, seek refuge with Allah from the evil of the devils of the jinn and mankind."" He said: O Messenger of Allah, do mankind have devils? He said: ""Yes, {The devils of mankind and jinn inspire one another with adorned speech as delusion} [Al-An'am: 112]."" Then he said: ""O Abu Dharr, shall I not teach you words from the treasure of Paradise?"" I said: Yes, may Allah make me your ransom. He said: ""Say: There is no power and no strength except with Allah."" I said: There is no power and no strength except with Allah. He said: Then he fell silent from me, so I waited for his speech. I said: O Messenger of Allah, we were people of ignorance and idol worship, then Allah sent you as a mercy to the worlds. What do you think about prayer, what is it? He said: ""It is a good deed placed; whoever wishes to do little may do little, and whoever wishes to do much may do much."" I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about fasting, what is it? He said: ""An obligatory duty that suffices."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, what about charity, what is it? He said: ""Manifold multiplied rewards, and with Allah is more."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, which charity is best? He said: ""A secret gift to a poor person, and the effort of one with little means."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, which of what was revealed to you is greatest? He said: ""{Allah, there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer} [Al-Baqarah: 255] — the Verse of the Throne."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, which martyr is best? He said: ""He whose blood is shed and whose horse is hamstrung."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, which slaves (to free) are best? He said: ""The most expensive in price and the most precious to their owners."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, which of the prophets was first? He said: ""Adam, peace be upon him."" I said: O Prophet of Allah, was Adam a prophet? He said: ""Yes, a prophet spoken to, created by Allah with His Hand, and He breathed into him of His Spirit, then He said to him: 'O Adam, go forth.'"" I said: O Prophet of Allah, how many prophets are there? He said: ""One hundred thousand and four and twenty thousand; the messengers from among them are three hundred and fifteen, a large multitude."" Narrated by Ahmad and al-Tabarani in al-Kabir, and he said: ""How many prophets are there?"" He said: ""One hundred thousand and four and twenty thousand."" And its chain rests on Ali ibn Yazid, and he is weak."
"726","On the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: ""I came to the Prophet — may Allah's peace and blessings be upon him — while he was in the mosque, so I sat down. He said: 'O Abu Dharr, have you prayed?' I said: No. He said: 'Stand and pray.' So I stood and prayed, then sat down. He said: 'O Abu Dharr, seek refuge with Allah from the evil of the devils of humans and jinn.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, do humans have devils? He said: 'Yes.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about prayer? He said: 'It is a good deed placed (before Allah); whoever wishes to do little may do so, and whoever wishes to do more may do so.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about fasting? He said: 'An obligatory duty that suffices, and with Allah there is more (reward).' I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about charity? He said: 'Multiplied rewards.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, which of them is best? He said: 'The effort of a person of little means, or a secret gift to a poor person.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the prophets was first? He said: 'Adam.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, was he a prophet? He said: 'Yes, a prophet spoken to (by Allah).' I said: O Messenger of Allah, how many messengers were there? He said: 'Three hundred and a few ten, a large multitude,' and he said once: 'Fifteen.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, was Adam a prophet? He said: 'Yes, spoken to.' I said: O Messenger of Allah, which verse revealed to you is greatest? He said: 'The Verse of the Throne (Ayat al-Kursi): {Allah — there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence} [Al-Baqarah: 255].' Narrated by Ahmad, Al-Bazzar, and Al-Tabarani in Al-Awsat similarly, and by Al-Nasa'i a portion of it. In its chain is Al-Mas'udi, who is trustworthy but became confused (in his later narrations). And in Al-Tabarani's version there is an addition that will come in the chapter on history."""
"727",""
