"949","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) was born on a Monday, received revelation on a Monday, migrated from Mecca to Medina on a Monday, arrived in Medina on a Monday, passed away (peace be upon him) on a Monday, and lifted the Black Stone on a Monday.Narrated by Ahmad and Al-Tabarani in Al-Mu'jam Al-Kabir, with the addition: ""And he conquered Badr on a Monday, and Surah Al-Ma'idah was revealed on a Monday: 'This day I have perfected for you your religion' [Al-Ma'idah: 3].""In its chain is Ibn Lahi'ah, who is weak, and the rest of its narrators are trustworthy, from the people of the Sahih."
"950",""
"951",""
"952",""
"953",""
"954","On the authority of Abu Dharr: He came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) while the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was delivering a sermon, so he sat down. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him: ""Have you sought refuge from the evil of the devils of jinn and men?"" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, who is the first of the prophets?"" He said: ""Adam."" I said: ""Was he a prophet?"" He said: ""Yes, one spoken to (by Allah)."" I said: ""Then who?"" He said: ""Noah, and between them there were ten forefathers."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, inform me about the prayer?"" He said: ""A good obligation; whoever wishes may increase it."" I said: ""Then charity?"" He said: ""Multiplied rewards."" I said: ""And fasting?"" He said: ""Fasting is a shield. Allah said: 'Fasting is for Me and I reward for it. And by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the breath of the fasting person is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk.'"" I said: ""Then which charity is best?"" He said: ""The effort of one with little means, and secretly to a poor person."" I said: ""Then which slaves (to free) are best?"" He said: ""The most expensive in price."" Narrated by al-Tabarani in al-Awsat. I say: It has been mentioned earlier that Ahmad narrated it and al-Bazzar in the chapter on asking for benefit, and in its chain is Ibn Lahi'ah, and he is weak."
